+### Local Pi delegated activity
+
+The local Pi integration can publish display-only `subagents_running` and
+`subagents_session_key` metadata (source `herdr:pi:subagents`). The key is the
+lowercase 64-character SHA256 hex digest of the full UTF8 SDK session file path.
+Native Herdr v0.9.3 limits each metadata value to 80 characters, so a full path
+in a token can be truncated; the digest fits without losing ownership identity.
+Radar accepts a positive decimal safe-integer count only for Pi with
+`agent_session.kind = "path"`, a nonempty native session value string, and an
+exact key match against SHA256 of that complete value. Missing, expired,
+malformed or foreign-session keys leave ordinary rendering unchanged. Legacy
+`subagents_session_path` tokens and truncated/shared path prefixes are not accepted.
+
+Optional `subagents_roles` metadata identifies the active children's roles. Only
+an owned positive count allows Radar to read this token: known codes are `A`
+(explore), `R` (research), `W` (worker), `V` (verify), and `RD` (background review).
+Distinct codes combine in that order (`A+W`); duplicates collapse. Tokens longer
+than 11 characters, malformed strings or any unknown code are rejected as a whole.
+Pi sidebar titles omit the exact leading textual `π - ` marker in every state,
+including the first entry that owns the separate original vendor logo. The working
+spinner and other activity indicators remain; other harnesses and embedded `π -`
+text are unchanged. The canonical terminal title is never renamed.
+In the blue delegated title, that leading marker becomes the validated codes plus
+one space: `A Inspect project structure`. Missing, empty or invalid roles show just
+the title words, so older producers still work without a misleading role prefix.
+A role change redraws even with the same count and title; completion clears blue
+and restores the plain title. No role is inferred from prompt text or agent labels.
+
+While children run, a confirmed idle-tier or held-finished parent's title uses
+the separate `$title_delegating` cell. Unknown parents never use it. The local sidebar config must provide that cell with
+blue foreground `#5F87FE`; Radar does not install it. Working and blocked titles
+keep precedence. Idle tiers and held finished badges keep their canonical state,
+and the finished green title returns when children stop. Logos, group layout,
+Spaces state and activity sorting do not change. The existing two-second daemon
+heartbeat reconciles metadata through the same scheduler; no extra polling loop
+or self-write `pane.updated` subscription is added. Pickup and clearing are not
+instant: allow up to five seconds under normal responsive operation. The producer
+design uses a 30-second metadata lease renewed every 10 seconds while children
+run. If the producer disappears without clearing, blue can remain until lease
+expiry plus reconciliation. No parent status is faked.
+
+This installed customization is update-sensitive: revalidate after plugin updates.
+Activation is separate from these edits; no live restart is performed here.
+
